# Executive Application Helper — starter .gitignore
#
# Copy to `.gitignore` at the workspace root before the baseline commit.
# The workspace is a git repository: that is what replaced the old
# snapshot-before-every-edit discipline. Commit at every session close that
# touched a tracked file, with a message that says what changed and why —
# under this model the commit message carries the reasoning that changelog
# entries used to, because entries are now only two to four lines.
#
# Setup:
#   cd "[Workspace Folder Path]"
#   git init
#   git config user.name  "[Candidate Name]"
#   git config user.email "[email]"
#   cp gitignore.template .gitignore
#   git add -A && git commit -m "Baseline: initial framework state"
#
# Recovery, replacing the snapshot folder entirely:
#   git diff                          # what changed since the last commit
#   git checkout -- <file>            # discard uncommitted damage to one file
#   git log --oneline -- <file>       # every state that file has had
#   git checkout <commit> -- <file>   # restore one file from any past commit

# Generated output — rebuildable from source, and noisy in diffs
Resume/*.pdf
Pipeline/*.pdf
Pipeline/*.docx
Pipeline/samples/

# Working scratch
outputs_work/
_scratch/

# Any pre-restructure archive kept on disk for reference but out of history
Archive_V5/
_resources/

# Documents staged for deletion
Submissions/_to_delete/

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
~$*
*.tmp
